&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About us&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div&gt;PhysicsX is a deep-tech company with roots in numerical physics and Formula One, dedicated to accelerating hardware innovation at the speed of software.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;We are building an AI-driven simulation software stack for engineering and manufacturing across advanced industries. By enabling high-fidelity, multi-physics simulation through AI inference across the entire engineering lifecycle, PhysicsX unlocks new levels of optimization and automation in design, manufacturing, and operations — empowering engineers to push the boundaries of possibility. Our customers include leading innovators in Aerospace &amp;amp; Defense, Materials, Energy, Semiconductors, and Automotive.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Opportunity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;PhysicsX is looking for a Senior Financial Accountant to join our growing finance team. This is a technically demanding role for a qualified accountant who is confident working across complex, multi-entity, multi-jurisdiction accounting — and who wants to take genuine ownership of the processes they run.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll be a key part of a team of four, reporting directly to the Finance Manager, and acting as the point of contact for group tax and statutory reporting across our UK, US, and Singapore entities. You&#39;ll work closely with external tax consultants, auditors, and advisers, and be expected to take clear ownership of the workstreams you lead.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a role for someone who thrives on responsibility, brings fresh thinking to improve processes and controls, and has the technical depth to navigate regulatory complexity across multiple jurisdictions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Revenue recognition&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leading global revenue recognition in line with FRS 102, ensuring accuracy and consistency with Group accounting policies across all entities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tax compliance and advisory&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supporting group tax compliance across the UK, US, and Singapore — acting as the main point of contact between the business and our external tax advisers, and helping to ensure corporation tax returns and year-end filings, including federal, state, and local obligations, are completed accurately and on time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Managing VAT and GST compliance obligations across jurisdictions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supporting R&amp;amp;D tax credit claims in collaboration with specialist advisers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Accounts receivable&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Owning the AR function end-to-end — including customer invoicing, cash allocation, and credit control — ensuring timely and accurate processing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Accounting &amp;amp; Standards&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintaining compliance with complex accounting standards across the group, including lease accounting (IFRS 16) and share-based payments (IFRS 2).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assessing and implementing new or amended standards as they come into effect, ensuring Group accounting policies remain current and consistent.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Acting as the internal point of reference for technical accounting queries across the business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Statutory and regulatory reporting&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leading timely and accurate statutory and regulatory reporting across the group, ensuring compliance with IFRS, UK GAAP, and relevant local standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Providing audit support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Controls and process improvement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Building and evolving a robust but agile financial controls framework — strong enough for scale and audit-readiness, without slowing the business down.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partnering with the wider organisation to embed smarter financial processes, helping teams understand and adopt improved ways of working.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identifying and implementing process improvements to strengthen controls, efficiency, and reporting quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Makes a Great Candidate&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
